like_any(x, P(pattern))(*) :-
  (~~docs
    The patterns in P that x is like, one row each. Under existence it is
    a test: +like_any(x & "a%"; "b%")(*) holds when x matches at least one
    pattern, and \+like_any(...)(*) when it matches none. Matching is
    like's: % stands for any run of characters and _ for one, and case
    follows the target's own LIKE. P's one column is read by position, so
    any single-column relation serves: +like_any(name, prefixes(*))(*).
    Without the mark it joins instead, and each row gains the pattern it
    matched, once per match. A NULL x matches no pattern, so \+like_any
    holds for it.
  ~~)
  P(*), +like($.x, pattern)
